[{"text":"GS[p] can be used as input for a 4-dimensional p^\\mu \\gamma_\\mu and is transformed into DiracGamma[Momentum[p]] by FeynCalcInternal (=FCI).","anchor":"gs"},{"text":"GS[p,q, ...] is a short form for GS[p].GS[q].","anchor":"gs"},{"text":"Overview, DiracGamma, GA, GAD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"GS[p]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[p] // FCI // StandardForm (*DiracGamma[Momentum[p]]*)","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[p, q, r, s]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{s}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[p, q, r, s] // StandardForm (*GS[p] . GS[q] . GS[r] . GS[s]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[q] . (GS[p] + m) . GS[q]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}+m\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"}]